            <ArticleTitle>Incorporating Trainees' Development into a Multidisciplinary Training Model for Integrated Behavioral Health Within a Pediatric Continuity Clinic.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>703-715</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1056-4993(17)30072-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.chc.2017.06.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Integrated behavioral and mental health systems of care for children require multidisciplinary team members to have specific competencies and knowledge of the other disciplines' strengths and practice needs. Training models for multidisciplinary professionals should consider the developmental level of trainees. The authors describe a model of flexible scaffolding, increasing intensity, and depth of experience as trainees gain skills and knowledge.</AbstractText>
